      "text": [
        " كَانَ أَبُو جَعْفَرٍ ( عليه السلام ) يَقُولُ لَا تَكُونُ الْخُطْبَةُ وَ الْجُمُعَةُ وَ صَلَاةُ رَكْعَتَيْنِ عَلَى أَقَلَّ مِنْ خَمْسَةِ رَهْطٍ الْإِمَامِ وَ أَرْبَعَةٍ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Ibn Azina, from Zurara who said, ",
          "‘Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> was saying: ‘Neither does the sermon take place, nor the Friday (<span class=\"iTxt\">Salāt</span>), and the two <span class=\"iTxt\">Rak’at</span> upon less that five persons, the prayer leader and four’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Ali has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from ibn ’Udhaynah from Zurarah who has said the following: “Abu Ja‘far, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘The sermons and Friday Salah (prayer) are not valid without the presence of five people, the fifth of whom is the Imam.’” "
        ]
      }
